```

Keep the controller method limited to that: validated input in, a model/action/service call, a response out. If the creation has real rules (pricing, inventory, events), move them into an action class or service method — e.g. `CreateOrder::handle($request->validated())` — rather than letting the controller grow past a couple of lines.

**4. Route** — route-model binding plus any route-specific middleware:

```php
